  "order": "Rotate the 18 canonical cases left by the round offset. For each case bracket the two diagnostic modes with a native control on each side. Latency-only goes first if canonical case index plus round index is even (both zero-based); bytes goes first otherwise.",
  "platform": "One temporary private Seoul N2D Compute Engine VM with one thread per core, matching the prior machine family and container image. Pin the container and workloads to guest CPU 1, housekeeping and observer to CPU 0. Compare both modes in the same candidate binary with x86-64-v2 CPUID, REP and latency enabled. Archive the actual build identities, guest placement and teardown receipts.",
