  "fit": "Fit nonnegative coefficients with no intercept by minimizing the summed squared relative errors on the six training case medians. Each feature is the median of three observations from the enabled mode. The native target is the median of the six wait4 observations. Score all three predictions against that target, with a case passing only if all three absolute errors are at most 20%. Recompute leave-one-program-out on the original five families: omit all scales of one family together. Transfer families are excluded from every fit. All programs have prior native timing data; this is a registered feature comparison, not blind algorithm selection.",
  "sensitivity": "Repeat the complete fit and scoring using the minimum of six native controls in place of their median. Keep the median primary. Report target shifts, pass counts and any quality-gate changes; retain short and high-spread observations.",
  "runtime_cost": "Report paired operand-enabled/latency-only wait4 CPU ratios by workload and mode order, plus the ratio of summed CPU times. Report instruction/latency changes between separate runs; do not assume identical dynamic startup paths. Do not equate instrumented CPU with native or production live-clock cost.",
